  <div style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:40px;">
    <div style="font-size:48px;margin-bottom:16px;">&#x1f6e1;</div>
    <h1 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:28px;font-weight:400;color:var(--text-1);margin-bottom:12px;">Responsible Use Policy</h1>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-3);line-height:1.7;">Penumbra Forge Security Labs are designed for education, training, and authorized security research. Please read this before starting.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="background:var(--surface-1);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;padding:32px;margin-bottom:24px;">

    <h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:18px;color:var(--text-1);font-weight:400;margin-bottom:16px;">What these labs are</h2>
    <ul style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-2);line-height:1.8;list-style:none;padding:0;">
      <li style="padding:6px 0;padding-left:24px;position:relative;"><span style="position:absolute;left:0;color:var(--sage);">&#x2713;</span> Educational tools for learning how vulnerabilities work</li>
      <li style="padding:6px 0;padding-left:24px;position:relative;"><span style="position:absolute;left:0;color:var(--sage);">&#x2713;</span> Safe, sandboxed environments running on isolated infrastructure</li>
      <li style="padding:6px 0;padding-left:24px;position:relative;"><span style="position:absolute;left:0;color:var(--sage);">&#x2713;</span> Practice environments for security professionals, students, and developers</li>
      <li style="padding:6px 0;padding-left:24px;position:relative;"><span style="position:absolute;left:0;color:var(--sage);">&#x2713;</span> References for understanding how to defend against real attacks</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:18px;color:var(--text-1);font-weight:400;margin:24px 0 16px;">What these labs are NOT</h2>
    <ul style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-2);line-height:1.8;list-style:none;padding:0;">
      <li style="padding:6px 0;padding-left:24px;position:relative;"><span style="position:absolute;left:0;color:#eb5757;">&#x2717;</span> Tools for attacking real systems, networks, or applications</li>
      <li style="padding:6px 0;padding-left:24px;position:relative;"><span style="position:absolute;left:0;color:#eb5757;">&#x2717;</span> Guides for unauthorized access to any system you don't own</li>
      <li style="padding:6px 0;padding-left:24px;position:relative;"><span style="position:absolute;left:0;color:#eb5757;">&#x2717;</span> Resources for developing malware, exploits, or attack tools</li>
      <li style="padding:6px 0;padding-left:24px;position:relative;"><span style="position:absolute;left:0;color:#eb5757;">&#x2717;</span> Authorization to test techniques against systems without explicit permission</li>
    </ul>
